BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208799@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261110T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T190000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Success Paradox 
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEve
 nt URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208799\n\n5:30PM Reception
 \, 6:00PM Discussion\nWhat happens when the success you have worked toward
  brings unexpected questions rather than fulfillment? Join psychiatrist an
 d author Dr. Blaise Aguirre for a keynote lecture exploring the emotional 
 complexities of ambition\, achievement\, and what comes next.\n\nDrawing o
 n research for his forthcoming book\, Dr. Aguirre will examine the imposte
 r phenomenon - the feeling that we have not earned our accomplishments - a
 nd the arrival fallacy\, the belief that reaching a goal will deliver last
 ing happiness. From “Do I deserve to be here?” to “How do I sustain 
 this?” and “What now?”\, he will explore the questions that can emer
 ge when high achievers reach the milestones they once imagined would be en
 ough.\n\nWith more than two decades of experience in mental health and as 
 founding medical director of 3East at McLean Hospital\, Dr. Aguirre brings
  a compassionate perspective to the pursuit of success. The conversation i
 nvites us to consider how we define achievement - and how greater self-und
 erstanding can help us build a life that feels as meaningful as it looks.\
 n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimenta
 ry light bites and refreshments will be served. Cancellations made within 
 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will result in a $25 charge
 .
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208799
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208800@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261110T183000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T200000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Old in the Game - A Reflection of Hip-Hop History 
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 12 spots left\nS
 tatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/20880
 0\n\n6:30PM Reception\, 7:00PM Discussion \nIn celebration of Hip-Hop His
 tory Month\, join author Murray Forman\, Boston hip-hop pioneer Edward “
 Edo.G” Anderson\, and Black music and culture scholar Emmett G. Price II
 I for a conversation about longevity\, identity\, and legacy in hip-hop.\n
 \nDrawing from Forman’s book Old in the Game: Aging In and With Hip-Hop
 \, the discussion will explore how the culture’s pioneering artists and 
 audiences navigate aging\, generational differences\, and the balance betw
 een honoring the past and creating what comes next. Edo.G brings the persp
 ective of a career spanning more than three decades\, from his breakthroug
 h with Ed O.G. and Da Bulldogs to enduring collaborations with Pete Rock a
 nd Masta Ace. Price adds his insight as a musician and scholar whose work 
 examines hip-hop’s cultural influence and the connections between genera
 tions.\n\nTogether\, they will consider what it means to grow older within
  hip-hop - and how the artists who helped define the culture continue to s
 hape its future.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members 
 only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. Cancellat
 ions made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will resul
 t in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208800
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-209103@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261111T163000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T180000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Instinct of Opportunity with Mellody Hobson 
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 7 spots left
 \nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/event
 s/209103\n\n4:30PM Reception\, 5:00PM Discussion\n\nJoin Sandy Edgerley\, 
 Co-Founder of The ’Quin House\, and Mellody Hobson\, Co-CEO of Ariel I
 nvestments\, for a conversation about leadership\, investment\, and the in
 stinct to see possibility before it becomes obvious.\n\nFrom guiding Ariel
 ’s growth to founding Project Level®\, Mellody has built a career arou
 nd ideas with the power to change industries. Together\, she and Sandy wil
 l explore what it takes to turn conviction into action\, with a closer loo
 k at the momentum behind women’s sports. As new audiences\, investment\,
  and influence reshape the field\, they will consider who gets to define i
 ts future—and what this moment reveals about opportunity in business.\n\
 n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary
  light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cance
 llations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209103
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-210561@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261111T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T193000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Liberation & Legacy - A Veterans Day Conversation
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 54 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/2
 10561\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion \nThis Veterans Day\, join 
 The ’Quin for a conversation honoring the American soldiers who liberate
 d Nazi concentration camps and the survivors whose lives they helped resto
 re.\n\nModerated by Jody Kipnis\, President and CEO of Holocaust Museum Bo
 ston\, the discussion brings together Mike Ross\, son of Holocaust survivo
 r Steve Ross\, who was liberated from Dachau\, and Jim Kelliher\, son of a
 n American soldier who helped liberate concentration camps.\n\nDrawing on 
 their fathers’ experiences\, a handwritten letter from May 1945\, and an
  original booklet documenting the 11th Armored Division\, the panel will e
 xplore liberation through the intertwined stories of those who survived an
 d those who came to their aid. Guests will also have the opportunity to vi
 ew Steve Ross’s flag and historical documents on display throughout the 
 evening\, offering a tangible connection to the lives and events at the he
 art of the conversation.\n\nTogether\, we will reflect on the courage and 
 service we honor on Veterans Day - and our shared responsibility to carry 
 these stories forward.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for me
 mbers only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. Can
 cellations made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will
  result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/210561
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-209680@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261111T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T203000
SUMMARY:Meet the Maker: Tom Gamble of Gamble Estates
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\n
 Event URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209680\n\nGreat wine be
 gins long before the first pour. Join Tom Gamble\, Founder and Vigneron of
  Gamble Estates\, for an exploration of Napa Valley through the lens of a 
 third-generation farmer. Begin with a welcome glass of 2025 Yountville Sa
 uvignon Blanc before discovering a selection of 2023 reds showcasing Mount
  Veeder\, Rutherford\, and Oakville. Along the way\, Tom will share how r
 egenerative farming\, a century of family roots\, and a collaboration with
  Atelier Melka shape wines that tell the story of their origins.\n\n*This 
 event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light
  bites and refreshments will be served. Cancellations made within 24 hour
 s of the event\, or failure to attend\, will result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209680
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
