SUMMARY:The Scottie's Sessions: Live Jazz with Northstar
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Avai
 lable\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208597\n\nSlip i
 nto Scottie’s for an evening of live jazz with an unexpected edge as Nor
 th Star takes the stage. Featuring tap\, tenor saxophone\, piano\, and bas
 s\, the quartet brings a playful twist to classic jazz\, with tap joining 
 the ensemble as both movement and percussion.\n\nGrab a cocktail\, settle 
 in\, and let the evening unfold—one beat\, note\, and step at a time.\n\
 nReservations are not required.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208597
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-209682@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261113T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T203000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Second Half of Athleticism - The Athlete's Dilemma
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 4 spots left
 \nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/20
 9682\n\n7:00PM Reception\, 7:30PM Discussion \nWhat happens when organize
 d competition ends\, but the athlete in us remains? For those who once bui
 lt their lives around practices\, teammates\, and seasons\, stepping away 
 can raise questions of identity\, purpose\, and how we care for ourselves 
 beyond the demands of competition.\n\nDr. Rich Joseph\, Harvard Medical S
 chool faculty physician and Founder of VIM Medicine\, returns to The ’Qu
 in to launch a three-part series exploring what it means to remain an athl
 ete for life. He will moderate a conversation with Marcus Wilson\, co-foun
 der of NOBULL\; Ben Bergeron\, founder of CompTrain and coach to multiple 
 CrossFit Games champions\; and Jeremy Bettle\, a performance and sports sc
 ience leader whose work spans professional sports and who now leads Vitali
 ty Collective.\n\nTogether\, they will explore how we redefine ambition\, 
 find new sources of motivation\, and build a lasting relationship with mov
 ement. It’s a candid look at life after the final whistle—and how the 
 discipline\, resilience\, and sense of possibility that shaped us as compe
 titors can continue to serve us for decades to come.\n\n*This event is com
 plimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and re
 freshments will be served. Cancellations made within 24 hours of the event
 \, or failure to attend\, will result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209682
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208334@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261114T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T120000
